========================================================================================================

  Your CDKTN TypeScript project is ready!

  cat help                Print this message

  Compile:
    {{ pmRun }} get           Import/update Terraform providers and modules (you should check-in this directory)
    {{ pmRun }} compile       Compile typescript code to javascript (or "{{ pmRun }} watch")
    {{ pmRun }} watch         Watch for changes and compile typescript in the background
    {{ pmRun }} build         Compile typescript

  Synthesize:
    cdktn synth [stack]   Synthesize Terraform resources from stacks to cdktf.out/ (ready for 'terraform apply')

  Diff:
    cdktn diff [stack]    Perform a diff (terraform plan) for the given stack

  Deploy:
    cdktn deploy [stack]  Deploy the given stack

  Destroy:
    cdktn destroy [stack] Destroy the stack

  Test:
    {{ pmRun }} test        Runs unit tests (edit __tests__/main-test.ts to add your own tests)
    {{ pmRun }} test:watch  Watches the tests and reruns them on change

  Upgrades:
    {{ pmRun }} upgrade        Upgrade cdktn modules to latest version
    {{ pmRun }} upgrade:next   Upgrade cdktn modules to latest "@next" version (last commit)

 Use Providers:

  You can add prebuilt providers (if available) or locally generated ones using the add command:
  
  cdktn provider add "aws@~>3.0" null kreuzwerker/docker

  You can find all prebuilt providers on npm: https://www.npmjs.com/search?q=keywords:cdktn
  You can also install these providers directly through {{ packageManager }}:

  {{ pmAdd }} @cdktn/provider-aws
  {{ pmAdd }} @cdktn/provider-google
  {{ pmAdd }} @cdktn/provider-azurerm
  {{ pmAdd }} @cdktn/provider-docker
  {{ pmAdd }} @cdktn/provider-github
  {{ pmAdd }} @cdktn/provider-null

  You can also build any module or provider locally. Learn more https://cdktn.io/docs/concepts/providers

